Anna (docs): Heads-up: I'm about to open a PR to update the Orpheus2b model card. Scope: clarify supported sequence limits for streaming vs non-streaming, add a tiny SDK snippet showing backoff+retry for 429s when hitting burst limits, and fix two stale links to the bench CSV and variant matrix. Need owners and a quick bench sentence.

Kira (eng-ml): SGTM. For Orpheus2b: non-stream generate limit is 8192 tokens (prompt+gen). Streaming accepts up to 16384 prompt tokens but we only stream tokens generated; note that very long prompts will cause memory pressure. Bench blurb: "Example: orpheus2b q4_1 warm p50 ~140ms, p95 ~380ms (eu-west, single-GPU)."

Ravi (eng-runtime): Note: Dedicated clusters sometimes set lower per-tenant caps; add Console link to check account overrides. Also the 429 body includes `retry_after_seconds` — show that in snippet.

Max (sdk): I'll draft the JS snippet for exponential backoff on 429 + small python equivalent. Want to include a note about upgrading to SDK >= 2.6.0 for the `retry_after_seconds` field?

Anna (docs): Yes please. Add a one-line migration note for users who imported the old variant names (orpheus-2b vs orpheus2b) — we canonicalized names so recommend checking the model_catalog alias list.

Max (sdk): JS snippet:
```js
const client = new RedwoodClient({ apiKey: process.env.RW_API_KEY });
async function generateWithRetry(req){
  let tries = 0;
  while(tries<4){
    try{
      return await client.generate(req);
    }catch(e){
      if(e.status===429){
        const wait = (e.body?.retry_after_seconds || Math.pow(2,tries)) * 1000;
        await new Promise(r=>setTimeout(r, wait));
        tries++;
        continue;
      }
      throw e;
    }
  }
  throw new Error('max retries');
}
```

Max (sdk): Python one-liner example for docs: `client.generate_with_backoff(request, max_retries=3)` — we'll add this helper in SDK soon.

